{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented as Gerrit change 2250 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2250\nCommit b71e46660fa6 on branch `fe4e-shellcheck-gate`. **Verified +1** (CI green);\nawaiting `LLM-Review`. Not closing until it is Verified +1 AND merged.\n\n## Corrections to this ticket's description\n\nImplementation disproved three claims in the original description. Recorded here\nrather than by editing it, so the trail keeps what was believed at filing time\nversus what turned out to be true.\n\n1. **\"shellcheck is neither installed nor in the lint gate\" — half wrong.**\n   `shellcheck-py==0.11.0.1` is ALREADY pinned exactly in pyproject's `[dev]` extra,\n   installed by `make install`, and `_build-and-test.yml` already runs a **gating**\n   \"ShellCheck 0.11.0 smoke check\" step. Only the lint-gate wiring was missing. That\n   made AC 4 (graceful degradation) and AC 6 (document the dependency) far lighter\n   than scoped, and made fail-closed unambiguously safe — CI already guarantees the\n   binary is present.\n\n2. **Workflow `run:` blocks were never ungated.** `make lint` runs actionlint, which\n   embeds ShellCheck for every `.github/workflows/**` step. The real gap was\n   standalone `*.sh` only — 35 files. The description implied no ShellCheck coverage\n   existed anywhere, overstating the hole.\n\n3. **The repo already runs mutation testing in CI** (`scripts/mutation_gate.py`,\n   `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml`) — a disposable environment, which is the\n   posture cargo-mutants explicitly recommends for destructive mutants.\n\n## What was built\n\n- `scripts/check_shellcheck.py` (118 LOC) — discovers `*.sh`, excludes vendored and\n  scratch trees, runs ShellCheck at `-S warning`, fails closed when the binary is\n  absent (matching `test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py`: \"shellcheck-py is a\n  required test dependency, not an optional skip\").\n- `tests/unit/test_check_shellcheck.py` (138 LOC, 12 tests) — pins AC 2 both ways:\n  `rm -rf \"${dir}\"/*` fails with SC2115, and the `: \"${dir:?}\"` +\n  `cd -- \"$dir\" && rm -rf -- ./*` form passes. Also asserts `SEVERITY == \"warning\"`,\n  because SC2115 is emitted at warning and a gate at `-S error` would run green over\n  the exact line that wiped /opt/homebrew.\n\n## The nine pre-existing findings\n\n- `infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` — six SC1083 on `^{commit}` git peeling\n  syntax. Fixed by quoting (`\"HEAD^{commit}\"`), not suppressed; quoting is correct\n  shell independent of the linter.\n- `infra/terraform/user_data.sh` — three justified line-scoped disables (SC2154,\n  SC2034, SC2066). It is a `templatefile()` source, so ShellCheck lints it pre-render\n  and resolves neither the Terraform interpolation nor the `$${...}` escaping. Genuine\n  false positives; the file stays gated for real future findings rather than excluded.\n\n## Verification\n\n`make lint` 0, `make typecheck` 0, complexity ratchet 0, 12/12 new tests pass.\n\n## Payoff\n\n`infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` is not on `main` — it exists only on the unmerged\n`fix-mcp-clone-blocks-boot` branch. When that lands, its\n`rm -rf \"${dir}\"/.[!.]* \"${dir}\"/*` line cannot merge without tripping SC2115.\n\nNote: posted via the local CLI — the MCP server did not expose `comment_ticket` to\nthis session. Same logical store (both sync `origin/tickets`)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787795574055091001,"uuid":"2cd160de-4387-427d-9fb4-991a29c1efd6"}